						<td class="headline" align="left"><a name="#886">Updated Guidelines for EMF</a></td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td class="body">
							Bare with me folks, this is going to be long!  If anyone has anything they think I need to add to the guildlines, please let me know!<br />
<br />
Charter:  We of the Elite Mystic Force are all family, bound by honesty, respect and friendship.  We are united for the good of fun and enjoyment as a group.  Those who have been accepted into the guild have proven their attitude, loyalty, dedication and faith to the family, and vow to remain honorable and uphold the good name of our guild.<br />
<br />
Guild Guildlines:<br />
<br />
1.  Guild Tag/Names:  Everyone will display the Guild Tag/Name on his or her character in game unless given permission by an offier for that gaming session.  There are times when someone needs to be ANON and not be able to be found or seen as part of the guild.  People while ANON will not communicate in guild chat unless there is a dire need, and then they will keep it to a minimum.<br />
<br />
2.  Don't overuse /shout or /ooc chat channels, including the guild channel (especially the guild chat).  As of this time Guild Chat channel isn't congested, as we don't have that many members on at any time.  If and when we grow to where the guild chat channel becomes congested we will have to find another means to harass/joke/poke fun at each other.<br />
<br />
3.  Try not to be rude, kill steal, or crash other people's camps.  It happens sometimes, but intentional behavior of this sort will result in expulsion from the guild.<br />
<br />
4.  Be honest in your dealings with others.  If asked to make a transfer for a stranger the choice is yours to oblige.  If you do this for someone don't cheat them or steal from them.  If a player does and is reported to the officers/guild leader and found to be guilty, the person and ALL their characters will be banned from the guild and all other guilds allied with EMF.  We will do our best to blacklist you from all guilds.<br />
<br />
5.  Treat all other members of the guild as equals, regardless of level.<br />
<br />
6.  Do NOT BEG from any other players for money or times.  Especially don't beg from other guild mates.  Feel free to ask questions and seek advice from the higher members, particularly an officer for your class if one is available.<br />
<br />
7.  Mainly, have fun and uphold the good name of your family, and try not to spoil anyone else's fun.  It happens once in a while, but try to treat other as you would be treated, with respect, honesty and good attitudes.<br />
<br />
8.  All members will register and keep their characters updated on this website.  If they are not registered and listed within 60 days of joining the guild, the members will be removed from the guild.  We also recommend checking the site once in a while for news and information that is being batted around.  Who knows, we may even schedule a surprise raid!<br />
<br />
9.  Guild structure and size restrictions.  In order to maintain the cohesive nature and family feeling of the guild, the following restrictions will take effect upon  the complete induction of players already introduced into the guild;<br />
<br />
a.  There is no minimum level for entrance to the guild at this time.  Low-level characters are fun too.<br />
<br />
b.  The total membership of the guild will not be restricted at this time.  (Primaries and secondaries combined)<br />
<br />
10.  The guild will establish a GUILD POOL of items and cash.  Items will be the results of raid and the cash will be the result of items sold from specific farming raids.  At time times the BANKER will be the Guild Leader's ALT character and will be equipped with containers to fulfill this role.<br />
<br />
11.  Raids and Raid Loot:  Players will earn Raid points for attending the few raids we happen to do.  The raid points will be used to roll for items in the guild pool.<br />
<br />
a.  First consideration will go to the class of raid-acquired items.<br />
<br />
b.  Gems, pages, runes and words acquired during a raid will be banked and distributed when any characters need them for reseach.  Priority will be given to clerics in the guild for gemstones needed for buffs during raids and the remainder will be rolled for using raid points when needed for jewelry skill building.<br />
<br />
c.  Raid points will be acquired during the raid for time spent at the raid (hehehe, a admin nightmare is raising it's ugly head).  For every 30 minutes at the raid actively participating, a player's character will get one point.  Actively participating can be anything to include; porting members for corpse runs back to raid area, healing/buffing raid members, escorting raid members, resurrecting raid memebers.  And anything else supporting the raid members that I forgot to put down here that takes time.<br />
<br />
12.  Recruiting:  We will always accept new members of any level if they prove to be of the same philosophy and exhibit honesty, generosity, fair play and camaraderie, the traits members members of EMF practice.  An invitation to guild membership will be extended to those that exhibit all the qualities that we (Elite Mystic Force) admire and practice in the game.  A trial period of 2 weeks to 30 days (needed because of exposure is paramount and some parts of the year officers cannot play as much as they would like) will be mandatory for any new candidates (not present members alternates) that are recruited into the guild.  If, during that time, the candidate proves to be of the quality of player we all practice and admire, then membership will be made permanent.  This also give the candidate a chance to see if they want to remain with us, as we (EMF) don't strive for daily raids or UBER guild status that some players have as goals.  We play to have fun with people we like, protecting our backsides in a group.<br />
<br />
Last and Foremost:  Most of the members of EMF are adults.  We are married, have kids, and have professions we pratice outside of Everquest to support our families and our EQ habit.  We are not here to build an UBER guild or have the best armor, weapons, equipment or plan and execute raids often to acquire that.  We don't have the time outside of our real lives and families.<br />
<br />
If you are looking or a guild that is constantly on the prowl for the best equipment, highest-level characters you can make and grinding to get to this level, then EMF is not the guild for you.  We are here to enjoy casual play, grouped with friends and acquaintances, and insult or rib each other for fun.  And we will also work for any equipment we can, but time isn't something most of us have, and EQ is a fun diversion to real life.  We may not have people beating down our recruitment door to get in because we can get anything in the game for them, but they will want to join because we are fun, honest, and care about the others in our family.<br />
<br />
Remember, we are here to share the fun and joy of virtual adventuring together.  Have fun and travel safe!
